    "explanation": "Both parties agree on the essential facts and the arithmetic is not seriously contested, so this is a money ruling rather than an escalation.\n\nRoute deviation (POL-RD-01). The governing measurement is the GPS trace, not the rounded trip-record copy: EV-GPS-00101 measures the trip at 27.18 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff, against a platform optimal of 21.0 km — an excess of 6.18 km, or 29.43%. Both establishment tests pass (more than 20% of optimal, and more than 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own evidence. It is NOT material: the excess is below the 50%-of-optimal threshold (10.5 km) and below 8.0 km absolute. POL-RD-06 is therefore not engaged by materiality, and in any event the driver's citable figures are deviation_flags_90d = 0 against completed_trips_90d = 812 (EV-DPROF-00101), a ratio of 0.00, so no repeat pattern, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral follow. The driver's lifetime prior_deviation_flags is a context-only near-synonym of the named trailing counter and is not used.\n\nExoneration and burden (POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-08). The rider has discharged her POL-RD-08 burden: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip TRP-00101, and the trace's first fix (10:21:05) matches the recorded start. The trace is unimpaired — 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s, no jump over 500 m — so POL-RD-07's impairment consequences never arise. No exculpatory clause answers the driver: the chat log contains no rider instruction to detour (no waypoint_hint is set and no road is named, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable), and no endpoint was amended (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, so POL-RD-05 does not apply). The driver's own admission — 'sorry boss missed the exit, coming back now' in the chat, and his counterparty statement that he took a wrong turn at the MCE exit — attributes the detour to him.\n\nFare recomputation (POL-RD-02). The fare is METERED. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 21.0 + 0.28 × 26.0) × 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee = 27.63. charged_total = 35.64. Refund = 35.64 − 27.63 = 8.01, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 8.05. That clears the 0.50 de minimis floor and is 22.47% of the charge, far short of the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of 8.05. The rider's filed figure of 10.00 is not supported by the arithmetic; the ceiling is 8.05. There are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines (the gantry list is empty, the ERP total 0.00), so POL-RD-09 adds nothing on top — any off-route pass-through would already be comprehended in the recomputation. There is no unbilled distance either (billed 27.2 km against trace 27.18 km), so no driver compensation arises.\n\nOne rider contention is not weighed: the assertion about the missing LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-00101-01) rests on a zero-weight MISSING artifact without disclosing its issue code, and is discarded under POL-GEN-02(1); the absence of an advisory is noted, but it carries no fact. Confidence is 0.90, capped by artifacts all at weight_multiplier 1.0 that carry the deciding facts."
